## Defence stack

The middleware is composed of four sequential defence layers plus one stretch goal. Each layer addresses a specific class of risk identified in the threat model.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Start([Incoming request])

    L1[Layer 1 - Input sanitisation<br/>Regex and keyword filters<br/>Catches obvious injection patterns]
    L2[Layer 2 - Structural separation<br/>Wrap untrusted data in delimiters<br/>Catches indirect injection from DB and CSV]
    L3[Layer 3 - PII redaction<br/>Presidio plus financial entity rules<br/>Catches PII leakage to third-party LLM]
    LLM[LLM API call<br/>External, OpenAI-compatible]
    L4[Layer 4 - Output validation<br/>Reject unauthorised actions or external URLs<br/>Catches action hijacking and exfiltration]
    L5[Layer 5 - Behavioural classifier<br/>Stretch goal - DistilBERT classifier<br/>Only if Layers 1 to 4 ship on time]
    Deferred[Deferred - guard models, constitutional AI<br/>Future work, out of scope for this paper]
    End([Validated response to user])

    Start --> L1 --> L2 --> L3 --> LLM --> L4 --> L5 --> Deferred --> End

    style L1 fill:#EAF3DE,stroke:#3B6D11
    style L2 fill:#EAF3DE,stroke:#3B6D11
    style L3 fill:#EAF3DE,stroke:#3B6D11
    style L4 fill:#EAF3DE,stroke:#3B6D11
    style L5 fill:#FAEEDA,stroke:#854F0B
    style Deferred fill:#F1EFE8,stroke:#5F5E5A
    style LLM fill:#FAECE7,stroke:#993C1D
```

### Layer summary

| Layer | Status | Effort | Defends against |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1. Input sanitiser | MVP | 1–2 days | Direct chat injection |
| 2. Structural separator | MVP | 1 day | Indirect injection from stored data |
| 3. PII redactor | MVP | 3–4 days | PII leakage across the API boundary |
| 4. Output validator | MVP | 2 days | Action hijacking, exfiltration |
| 5. Behavioural classifier | Stretch | 5–7 days | Novel or obfuscated injection |

## Threat model

The defence stack responds to five attack vectors specific to LLM-powered personal finance applications. The full threat model lives in [`threat-model.md`](./threat-model.md) (forthcoming).

## Provider independence

The middleware does not depend on any specific LLM provider. The reference implementation uses an OpenAI-compatible chat completion endpoint, configurable via environment variables. See [`.env.example`](../.env.example) for configuration.